---
import Base from "~/layouts/Base.astro";
import { loadEnrichedImages } from "~/lib/images";

const count = (await loadEnrichedImages()).length;

const principles = [
  {
    title: "Official sources",
    text: "Each image starts from what the distribution publishes, verified against its own checksums or keys. No third-party base, no hidden layer.",
  },
  {
    title: "Minimal, identical changes",
    text: "Only what a cloud image needs: one cloud-init policy, guest agent, serial console, cleanup. The same rules for every distribution, documented per image.",
  },
  {
    title: "Verifiable",
    text: "Built in public CI, signed with Sigstore cosign by the build workflow itself, with a provenance manifest for every file.",
  },
  {
    title: "Tested where it runs",
    text: "Each release boots on a real OpenStack cloud and must pass the same checks before it is considered good.",
  },
  {
    title: "Always current",
    text: "Images follow upstream releases automatically, every day, instead of whenever someone has time.",
  },
  {
    title: "Open",
    text: "All the tooling is GPL-2.0 on GitHub. Fork it, audit it, or run the same pipeline for your own images.",
  },
];
---

<Base
  title="About"
  description="Why Open Image Cloud exists: signed, tested and current cloud images for OpenStack and Proxmox, built from official sources."
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-14 sm:px-6 sm:py-20">
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1 class="text-ink mt-3 text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight">
      Cloud images you do not have to rebuild yourself
    </h1>
    <p class="text-ink-muted mt-4 text-lg leading-relaxed">
      Running OpenStack or Proxmox means maintaining a shelf of base images: downloading them from a
      dozen projects, each with its own format, default user, cloud-init quirks and release rhythm,
      then checking that they still boot. Open Image Cloud does that work once, in the open, for{" "}
      {count} images, and publishes the result in one place with one set of rules.
    </p>

    <section class="mt-14">
      <h2 class="text-ink text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Principles</h2>
      <dl class="mt-6 grid gap-6 sm:grid-cols-2">
        {principles.map((p) => (
          <div class="border-line rounded-xl border p-5">
            <dt class="text-ink font-medium">{p.title}</dt>
            <dd class="text-ink-muted mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed">{p.text}</dd>
          </div>
        ))}
      </dl>
    </section>

    <section class="text-ink-muted mt-14 leading-relaxed">
      <h2 class="text-ink text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Who it is for</h2>
      <p class="mt-3">
        Cloud operators who publish public images to their users, teams running private OpenStack or
        Proxmox clusters, and anyone who wants a known-good, verifiable image to start from.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="text-ink-muted mt-14 leading-relaxed">
      <h2 class="text-ink text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">How it runs</h2>
      <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5">
        <li>One repository per image, all sharing the same build workflows on GitHub Actions.</li>
        <li>
          Files stored on Infomaniak Object Storage in Switzerland, served worldwide through
          Cloudflare.
        </li>
        <li>
          Machine-readable catalog at{" "}
          <a class="link" href="https://images.openimages.cloud/index.json">
            index.json
          </a>
          , plus an export for the osism openstack-image-manager, so updates can be automated.
        </li>
        <li>
          Every image is tested before and after publication:{" "}
          <a class="link" href="/quality/">
            see what is checked
          </a>
          .
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="text-ink-muted mt-14 leading-relaxed">
      <h2 class="text-ink text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">What it is not</h2>
      <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5">
        <li>
          Not affiliated with the distributions it packages. Their names and logos belong to their
          owners, and each image keeps its upstream license.
        </li>
        <li>
          Not a commercial service: images come as they are, without a support contract. Problems
          are tracked in public on GitHub.
        </li>
        <li>No proprietary system images we are not allowed to redistribute.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="text-ink-muted mt-14 leading-relaxed">
      <h2 class="text-ink text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Next</h2>
      <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5">
        <li>
          <a class="link" href="https://github.com/open-img-cloud/oic-sync">
            oic-sync
          </a>
          , the tool that imports and keeps images up to date in OpenStack, is out; Proxmox support
          comes next.
        </li>
        <li>OPNsense, built on the FreeBSD pipeline.</li>
        <li>
          Testing every release before the <code class="font-mono text-sm">latest/</code> alias
          moves.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p class="mt-6">
        Missing an image?{" "}
        <a class="link" href="https://github.com/open-img-cloud/.github/issues">
          Open a request
        </a>
        . Want to help? See the{" "}
        <a class="link" href="/sponsors/">
          sponsors page
        </a>
        .
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</Base>
